{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/939446-why-killing-is-breaking-point-of-integrity","id":939446,"title":"Why killing is Breaking Point of Integrity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T04:38:15-07:00","id":939446,"title":"Why killing is Breaking Point of Integrity","content":"Great video explaining why, for most humans, killing other man is really hard psychologically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zViyZGmBhvs\" data-code=\"zViyZGmBhvs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zViyZGmBhvs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T22:45:30-07:00","id":939965,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of Foster's 'Book of the Damned' series starting with 'Call to Arms', in it humanity joins a war in space and discovers that it comes easy to them because they are killing aliens, not humans.<br /> So, should it still be a breaking point to kill inhuman monsters?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T00:51:29-07:00","id":939991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/939446-why-killing-is-breaking-point-of-integrity?p=939965#post939965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, should it still be a breaking point to kill inhuman monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Does killing animals is Breaking Point?</b> I would say that first, or maybe even first three times it is. There are examples showing that father takes little son on hunting and junior cannot pull it off, crying doing the deed. Hell, it's even in game play trailer for 2016 <b>God of War</b> game ( see from 7:45 )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJ_GCPaKywg\" data-code=\"CJ_GCPaKywg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/CJ_GCPaKywg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> If animals are problem, it can be made point that aliens are also living and thinking beings. BUT, on the other hand, genere narration need antagonists and game session plot need some combat action. In that case, it's all based on ST decision.<br /> <br /> Myself, I would let all character just kill aliens. Maybe PCs very sheltered would have Breaking Point or two for first time - as popular trope in genere <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ItGetsEasier\" target=\"_blank\">It Get's Easier</a> - but from then, any 'monster hunter' does not is shaken by putting away Cthulhu. They are <i>monsters</i>, in the end.<br /> <br /> Problem still could be more human-looking monsters ( like vampires, werewolves or changelings ) because they<i> look</i> so much like normal people, rising this 'I need to <i>not</i> kill human kind' instinct that was in my OP video. Even then, I would probably lower Breaking Point penalty by half ( to -3 ) for killing 'almost humans'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T04:43:28-07:00","id":940048,"title":"","content":"All of these arguments are predicated on the assumption that you see the enemy as human in the first place. Throughout history, there's a deliberate brainwashing by many armies to teach their soldiers to see the enemy not as human, but as something less. This creates a far more different sitation than the one presented. <br /> <br /> Conversely, when you see an animal as human (placing human-like traits onto non-human animals and objects is a trait of the human race), then killing an animal may cause a psychological reaction as well.<br /> <br /> As well, killing in the CofD is not the same thing as killing on a battlefield. There's a lot going on here, emotional investments that completely change the psycholgical perspective. From a criminology standpoint, there are lots of people who kill another, feel no regret or remorse from it, and have absolutely no inclination to kill anyone else, returning to a functional and productive member of society.<br /> <br /> These all depend on the individuals in question. There are no blanket answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T08:46:01-07:00","id":940093,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a>, did you watched video from Opening Post? It nicely sums up most that you wrote - only that people in general situation ( outside of battle conditions ) will treat other persons as 'human being' and subconsciously will try to miss. Army try to brainwash you to shoot before hesitation kicks in, but even this is not 100% sure. This even goes in to <i>more</i> PTSD for soldiers and other fighters as they need to cope with consequence of killing other human without considering it in the first place.<br /> <br /> I was even thinking about new Merit like <i>Combat Instinct</i> ( or something ) that would give you no need to automatic roll on Breaking Points in fight situation for soldiers and like - but then I understood it would be no benefit when almost all Breaking Points rolls are roll between scenes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T18:26:49-07:00","id":940372,"title":"","content":"I did. As someone involved in criminology, however, I can tell you the video is not really applicable in the way you're thinking. Not for a typical CofD setting. There are psychological vectors in play in a domestic horror setting that are vastly different from what's been portrayed here. The video doesn't reflect what happens with real world murders and the effects on their minds. The overwhelming majority of the video showcases why people will hesitate to pull a trigger and shoot someone after military training. It does not touch on how a husband will feel after beating his wife to death, or self defense, or other situations likely to happen in a domestic setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, PCs aren't average people. They very well include the type of people that can be a sniper and go on without an issue. They can be anywhere on the psychological spectrum, with a high instance of being rare types rather than average. In fact, I argue that the very nature of a person that lets them see past all the Quintessences and Masquerades that the average person can't / won't makes any attempts to categorize PCs as &quot;average&quot; or &quot;most&quot; as an exercise in futility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-30-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T19:01:25-07:00","id":940385,"title":"","content":"Remember that for many people, putting you in a car where they can't see your face (or on internet) is enough to make your brain forget they are &quot;human like you&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}